{
  "id": "ds169",
  "snapshot": "data_science",
  "instruction": "You can open Visual Studio Code and create a Python script named `credit_approval_visualization.py` in the `/home/user/analysis_results/` directory. The dataset `credit_approval.csv` is already located in the same directory. In this script, load the dataset using pandas and create two visualizations: (1) a bar chart showing the average `A14` (credit amount) by `A9` for each approval class (`+` or `–`), saved as `credit_amount_bar.png`; and (2) a boxplot showing the distribution of `A2` values for approved vs. rejected applications, saved as `a2_boxplot.png`. Label all axes, legends, and titles clearly, and save both charts in the same directory. Finally, create a single slide in Microsoft PowerPoint that includes both visualizations and clearly communicates the key insights and overall story shown by the charts.",
  "source": "openml://29",

  "config": [
    {
      "type": "command",
